WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.224 --> 00:00:03.510
-- [Woman] When you aren't a
first mover in an industry,

00:00:03.510 --> 00:00:07.575
like Wine Library TV was, or a
social channel like Instagram,

00:00:07.575 --> 00:00:10.978
Facebook, Twitter which all have
so many people on them now,

00:00:10.978 --> 00:00:14.529
how do you go about
breaking through the noise?

00:00:14.529 --> 00:00:16.617
- Talent.

00:00:18.818 --> 00:00:20.968
(audience laughter)

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:22.122
- Some of the
questions will be short.

00:00:22.122 --> 00:00:25.492
- You know why, (laughs),
you know why I'm excited?

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:28.562
I'm excited because I have a
lot of respect for this room.

00:00:28.562 --> 00:00:30.731
There's a lot of
talent in this room.

00:00:30.731 --> 00:00:35.102
Just 'cause you weren't first,
doesn't mean you can't be best.

00:00:35.102 --> 00:00:37.337
Now remember, 
best comes in two-fold.

00:00:37.337 --> 00:00:38.805
It's why I made that point.

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:41.475
If you're actually great at
what you do for a living,

00:00:41.475 --> 00:00:42.709
that's only part of it.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:45.312
You have to be great 
at communicating it

00:00:45.312 --> 00:00:47.948
in the way it's 
communicated today.

00:00:47.948 --> 00:00:51.585
You have to understand angles
and pictures or what works in

00:00:51.585 --> 00:00:53.553
video or how to use hashtags to

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:56.857
be discovered when nobody
knows who you are.

00:00:56.857 --> 00:00:58.982
They both matter but shouldn't

00:00:58.982 --> 00:01:01.981
you put in the work if 
you get the benefit?

